  "notes": [
    "M1 D-A: the CloseSession engine is the caller's attached engine (actors/0/engine = E1), not state.current_engine. In both close-session-retired-engine cases E1 is RecoveryConfirmedRetired while current_engine E2 is Admitting, so the class is LocalReleaseAndHandoff cleanup3/commit255 (wire-v2 class table, coordinator D-A); reading current_engine would wrongly give the Admitting whole-abort class.",
    "M2 D-A handoff set = live RW/Recovery of the Outstanding obligations whose origin_session is the caller session. O1 is RecoveryConfirmed (not Outstanding, O(E) definition 'Outstanding만', readset-v2 O(T)/O(E) row) and its owners are Released, so no handoff row and no obligation row. The LocalReleaseAndHandoff path carries no RW(T) release, so in the open-shell workspace commit stays 255 and the Ended RW T1 contributes only transaction=[6,0,255,1,1,1,0].",
    "M3 Post-recovery history choices in supplement2:retired-engine-after-recovery that the assembler does not read: CloseSession clears actor.transaction and leaves slot0 Vacant (statement Retired/SessionClose, binding Released); T1 becomes life Ended after Recovery; SessionCleanup/RecoveryConfirmed fact payload fields (decision NotApplicable, consumed_parts 2) are plausible fills. Recovery's precondition (both shells Closed) holds, so this state is history-shaped; the open-shell variant is explicitly a non-reachable read-set workspace.",
    "M4 D-B: FinishCommit NCR takes cleanup3 + exact handoff only when the attached engine admission is Fenced (wire-v2 'Fenced이면3 아니면2'). A RecoveryConfirmedRetired engine (workspace) gives cleanup2 plus the first-fence census of that engine, identical in shape to the Admitting asm/pc-BeforeAttempt/1520. NOTE: devdoc/contracts/dev4-lifecycle-assembler.md section '구현 해석과 자원' still says the Fenced branch of CloseSession Complete AND Finish NCR applies whenever admission is not Admitting; that matches D-A but contradicts D-B for Finish NCR. I applied the coordinator-relayed D-B; the contract line needs updating.",
    "M5 Finish NCR Fenced handoff (owner-scope-v2 A5: 'Finish NCR의 이미 Fenced 분기는 handoff 행이며 cause raw NCR로 기존 O값을 덮지 않는다'; D-C): the parked T's existing O is a peer O created by actor1's fence, so the handoff row keeps known_decision NotAttempted, not NCR. Only that T's live RW3+Recovery are handed off (before=T, after=O, Transferred, count4/AllTransferred); actor1's O/owners and actor0's Plan/Binding are not part of the envelope.",
    "M6 Matching ParkedCommit copies the original context and the three control fields exactly (proposal section 4: matching이면 original deadline·cancel/reached 두 bit 복사): (FutureAtEntry, cancel=true, reached=false) and (FutureAtEntry, cancel=false, reached=true). The fact candidate still uses the caller attached engine E1 and next Fact.",
    "M7 Census order in supplement2:peer-fenced-parked-commit follows the contract's transaction identity-key order (supplement N1): actor0's T n1 (session1) before actor1's T n2 (session2), so O actor0 n1 / Recovery u9, O actor1 n2 / Recovery u10. Here nonce and key order coincide; the pre-state only needs them to be coherent.",
    "M8 D-C CommitAtomic on a fenced RW T with Outstanding O1 (original rw.recovery_pending, prior_successful_write true): recipe is RW(T) release only, so Recovery u6 is excluded. The rows link O1 and O1's row is included (contract: 'T에 기존 O가 있으면 그 T의 RW/Recovery row는 O를 연결하고 연결 row가 있을 때 O row를 포함'). Count/summary are envelope-local, 3/AllReleased. Success changed-RW Published supplies Committed; ValidationAborted keeps the existing NotCommittedRecoveryRequired. The Success receipt is new in T's scope [8,0,255,1,1,1,0] (T.receipt was None, next Receipt 1) with anchor [12,255,255,1,0,1,0]. The model's fence gate may reject both; supplied bytes are unaffected (authentication is not admission).",
    "M9 CloseSession Incomplete with caller T None runs the peer census (readset-v2 section 4: 'caller T=None이더라도 Incomplete의 peer census를 임의 생략하지 않는다'; coordinator). There is no cause T, so the peer's new O uses T.decision NotAttempted. Commit class is the fixed NCR1 and transaction is None. The caller's own Plan/Binding are not released (wire-v2: 'local 성공을 발명하지 않음').",
    "M10 Unmatched continuations follow A2 (owner-scope-v2; readset-v2 section 5): no pending, or a pending of the other kind (ParkedFetch for FinishCommit), gives context None, control (Absent,false,false), transaction None (never actor.transaction), owners/O empty and no census even with live RW transactions. The wrong-kind payload is not read or copied. The raw class (Finish Unknown: cleanup 255, commit 7, no receipt) and the fact candidate remain.",
    "M11 Peer transactions after a fence are modelled as life RecoveryPending with decision unchanged (same as supplement N9). Peer O have creation_reason PeerActiveTransactionAtFence and reason_mask 8. A BeforeAttempt parked T keeps progress BeforeAttempt and its parked_context backlink.",
